{"book":{"id":"book-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham","slug":"possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham","title":"Possessing Genius: The Bizarre Odyssey of Einstein's Brain","authors":[{"id":"person-carolyn-abraham","name":"Carolyn Abraham"}],"publisherId":"publisher-icon-books","imprintId":"imprint-icon-books","isbn13":["9781840466256"],"subjects":["Science"],"topics":["Essays & Cultural Criticism","Medicine, Health & the Body","Family, Childhood & Adoption"],"centralFigures":["Thomas Stolz Harvey"],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Possessing%20Genius%3A%20The%20Bizarre%20Odyssey%20of%20Einstein's%20Brain%20Carolyn%20Abraham","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Possessing%20Genius%3A%20The%20Bizarre%20Odyssey%20of%20Einstein's%20Brain%20Carolyn%20Abraham","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Possessing%20Genius%3A%20The%20Bizarre%20Odyssey%20of%20Einstein's%20Brain%20Carolyn%20Abraham","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Possessing%20Genius%3A%20The%20Bizarre%20Odyssey%20of%20Einstein's%20Brain%20Carolyn%20Abraham","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9009920W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-governor-generals-english-nonfiction-wikipedia-governor-general-s-award-for-english-language-non","source-cover-open-library-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham","source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham","source-imprint-edition-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham","source-imprint-normalization"],"thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham.jpg","experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Thomas Stolz Harvey","confidence":0.82}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Princeton Hospital","confidence":0.78}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The brain’s decades in Thomas Stolz Harvey’s possession show how scientific investigation and celebrity-driven curiosity together shaped what people believed made genius and “what we believe makes us human.”","confidence":0.66},"academicOrientation":{"score":45,"confidence":0.4},"profileConfidence":0.73,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Einstein","confidence":0.55}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"c1b36a5f783fecff95e36a4e2cf4700a38dd2df82794d0c94c53087fd13bdfa9","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Science","secondarySubjects":["Biography"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily explores the scientific legacy and unique circumstances surrounding Einstein's brain, framing it within a biographical context.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"621410feab50ed91018f3e8be8a882825b208b777ee9c060c0899b3a42dca0eb","summary":"\"The story began in April 1955, when Thomas Stolz Harvey, chief pathologist at Princeton Hospital, found himself in charge of dissecting the cadaver of the greatest scientist of his age, perhaps of any age. He seized the opportunity to do something \"noble.\" Using an electric saw, Harvey sliced through the skull and gingerly removed the organ that would both define and haunt the rest of his life. Harvey struck a controversial deal with Einstein's family to keep the brain, swearing to safeguard it from souvenir hunters and publicity seekers, and to make it available only for serious scientific inquiry. Not a neuroscientist himself, he became the unlikely custodian of this object of intense curiosity and speculation, and the self-styled bulwark against the relentless power of Einstein's growing celebrity.\". \"Bridging the postwar era and the new millennium, Possessing Genius is the first comprehensive account of the circuitous path the brain took during the decades it remained in Harvey's possession. Harvey permitted Einstein's gray matter to be sliced, diced, probed, prodded, and weighed by those hoping to solve the enigma and locate the source of genius itself. The brain was more than a subject of scientific investigation, it was a kind of holy relic; the history of its adventures since 1955 reflects the vicissitudes and vanities underpinning what we believe makes us human.","publicationYear":2001,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Neurosciences","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Pathologists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Dissection","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Brain","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Einstein, albert, 1879-1955","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Brain, localization of functions","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brain-carolyn-abraham"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Brain, research","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-possessing-genius-the-bizarre-odyssey-of-einstein-s-brai